The test method computes `to_numpy_dispatch` from Python's randomized `hash()` on two strings, so the boolean can vary across separate process executions. In `abs_max_quantize`, line 75 branches on `if to_numpy:`. The `True` branch executes lines 77–88 and returns via the NumPy path, while the `False` branch executes lines 91–100 and returns via the tensor ops path. Because the question asks whether the ordered line-number sequence is exactly identical across repeated executions, and the test itself can select either branch depending on the hash-derived boolean, the path is not guaranteed to be the same across runs. The oracle parser also compares full extracted line-number sequences for equality across runs, so any branch difference breaks the invariant.

